      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">The Database Safari</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6">Exploring Vector, Time-Series, Graph, Columnar/OLAP, and Geospatial Databases in the Wild</p>
      <p><em>The Database Safari</em> is a practical field guide to the wild world beyond traditional SQL and NoSQL. Journey through columnar, lakehouse, event-stream, time-series, probabilistic, vector, graph, and geospatial databases to discover how each is engineered, where it excels, and what trade-offs it brings. Grounded in real-world workloads and architectural patterns, the book cuts through the hype to help developers, architects, and data engineers recognize when a general-purpose database is enough—and when a specialist has truly earned its place. The result is a clear, workload-first guide to building intentional hybrid data architectures that are fast, scalable, and operationally sustainable.</p>

